    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining the offensive core, serving as our strongest plays. Despite **Gunnar Henderson** facing a formidable arm in Gerrit Cole (xERA 3.46), his robust base projection of 60.65 and the benefit of hitting out of the three-hole drive his score to a team-high 74.74. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable park factor and a soft matchup against Kyle Bradish (xERA 4.31), pushing his efficiency to 73.66. **Sam Antonacci** is our surprise upside candidate at 67.67; while his base projection is modest, his leadoff spot and a exploitable matchup against G. Holmes make him a critical asset for runs and stolen base potential.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal slot occupied by **Coby Mayo**, who narrowly outpointed **Nasim Nunez** despite the latter's immense speed upside. While **Nasim Nunez** (36.77) was a candidate to start due to our prioritization of stolen bases, the optimizer ultimately penalized him heavily for a bottom-of-the-order assignment and an brutal matchup against Jacob deGrom. **Coby Mayo** (45.87) secures the UTIL spot primarily on the back of his park factor, though he remains a high-risk play facing the Gerrit Cole-led rotation. Meanwhile, **Wade Meckler** (48.71) sits on the cusp of our \"Strong\" tier; he remains in the lineup based on his projected leadoff duties, but his ceiling is capped by a lack of elite power metrics.\n\nRisk management remains paramount today, particularly with several lineups still listed as \"Pending.\" We are monitoring **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Coby Mayo** closely; if any of these players are shifted down in their respective batting orders, their efficiency scores will plummet, potentially triggering a mid-day pivot. We are also managing our game caps with discipline, choosing to keep **Nasim Nunez** on the bench rather than chasing stolen base production against a dominant arm like Jacob deGrom. Our path to a successful Roto session relies on **Miguel Vargas** capitalizing on his strong 0.382 xwOBA against G. Holmes to bridge the production gap in the middle of our order.",
